  "summary": "The study compares six Ti3C2Tx-based electrodes: five NaBF4/HCl-etched temperature variants (MX-25, MX-60, MX-80, MX-100, and MX-130) and an HF-etched control (MX-HF). MX-130, prepared by NaBF4/HCl etching at 130 \u00b0C, is the headline and best-performing material, delivering 262 F g\u22121 at 1 A g\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4 in a three-electrode cell. The authors also fabricated a commercial RuO2 positive electrode for asymmetric-device balancing; it delivered 488 F g\u22121, though the associated current density is not stated in the supplied text. No electrode mass loadings, thicknesses, BET surface areas, porosities, or areal/volumetric capacitances are reported in the supplied paper text."
